// endpoint_evaluate_in_editor.proto — EvaluateInEditor: evaluate elisp in the
// running editor and answer with the result. EDITOR section.
//
// ONE ROUND TRIP. The daemon pushes the text to the editor serving the named
// workspace (agentrepl.v1.WatchHostWorkspaceResponse.evaluate, carrying a fresh
// EditorEvaluationToken), the editor evaluates it in its one handler with the
// workspace's buffer current, answers with AnswerEditorEvaluation, and this
// rpc returns that answer. An editor that does not answer within the
// evaluation deadline is `timed_out`; its late answer is discarded.

